<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caribbean</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Caribbean is the region of islands and coasts surrounding the Caribbean Sea, colonised by European powers from the late fifteenth century. Its plantation economies, worked by enslaved Africans, many from regions such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a>, made it a centre of the Spanish, British and French empires. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s victories in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a> confirmed it as the dominant colonial power there, and Caribbean movements such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rastafari">Rastafari</a> later looked to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> as a symbol.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caribbean.jpg" alt="Caribbean" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Central Intelligence Agency (CIA) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
